From cd0eeed012d4fc1a0437d1dc4e9c8fca80c021fd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: T0 <dev@local>
Date: Wed, 5 Aug 2026 09:38:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] T3: transfer and disposal repositories, UoW wiring, Result<T>
 transaction overload

Data-access layer for API 4.10. No orchestration logic yet - that's T5.

- IUnitOfWork.ExecuteInTransactionAsync<TValue> (fix F5): value-returning
  overload with identical rollback/commit semantics, so receive and create
  can return a summary out of the transaction without the closure-capture
  workaround BatchUploadService uses today.
- ICardTransferRepo / CardTransferRepo: paged list (BranchId matches either
  source or target, per the API 4.10 scope note), detail (full includes),
  GetForUpdateAsync (tracked, for settlement), HasInProgressTransferAsync
  (pre-built for BranchService's stock guard in T6).
- ICardDisposalRepo / CardDisposalRepo: same shape, scoped to disposals.
- IStockRepo.GetManyForUpdateAsync: tracked multi-key lookup so settling a
  multi-line transfer isn't N round trips. Composite-key IN-clause EF can't
  translate, so narrows by two IN-lists then exact-matches client-side -
  fine at transfer-line cardinality.
- IProductItemRepo.GetManyForUpdateAsync: tracked lookup by id list with
  explicit !IsDeleted (F1's chosen mitigation - no query filter exists on
  this entity).
- IProductItemRepo.GetAvailableForUpdateAsync: FIFO card selection by
  branch+product+status, used for Unknown-way create and by-quantity
  standalone disposal.

Correction to CardTransferItem's T1 doc comment: rows are written for
Unknown-way lines too, selected by the system via GetAvailableForUpdateAsync,
never supplied by the caller. ERD 8's 'not enumerated' describes the API
surface, not the internal bookkeeping - settling a line still requires
knowing exactly which physical cards moved. TransferDetailResponse.Items
continues to omit them for Unknown-way lines at the projection level (T5).

Verified: every TransferListFilter and DisposalListFilter field is read by
its repo, and nothing is read that isn't declared on the DTO.
